 "operation": [
  {
   "topic": "Polarity",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "Each type comes unidirectional (A suffix), marked with a colour band at the cathode, or bidirectional (CA suffix), with no band. Both share one row of the electrical table, except that at VRWM of 10 V or below the bidirectional IR limit is doubled. The forward surge rating (Fig. 6) is for unidirectional parts only."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Pulse rating",
   "page": 4,
   "text": "The 600 W minimum holds for a 10/1000 µs pulse at a repetition rate (duty cycle) of 0.01 %: a 10 µs rise to peak, then a decay that reaches half the peak at 1 ms (Fig. 3). Each part's maximum clamping voltage VC is given at its own peak pulse current IPP for that pulse. Shorter pulses allow more power: about 11.6 kW at 1 µs, falling to about 0.5 kW at 1000 µs (Fig. 1), with 5.0 mm × 5.0 mm copper pads."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Derating",
   "page": 4,
   "text": "Peak pulse power and current are at 100 % at TA = 25 ℃ and fall linearly to zero at 150 ℃ (Fig. 2). Steady state dissipation PM(AV) is 5.0 W at 50 ℃ and falls linearly to zero at 150 ℃ (Fig. 5)."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Forward surge",
   "page": 4,
   "text": "A unidirectional part takes 100 A for a single 8.3 ms half sine; the allowed peak falls with the number of 60 Hz cycles to about 25 A at 100 cycles (Fig. 6)."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Leakage and capacitance",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "Typical IR is under 1 µA for parts above 10 V; the table maximum is 1 µA from SMBJ11A up and rises to 800 µA at the 5.0 V and 6.0 V parts. Junction capacitance falls as breakdown voltage rises; with no bias it is a few nF at the lowest voltages and tens of pF at the highest, and the unidirectional part has more than the bidirectional one (Fig. 4). At reverse bias VR it is lower again, falling to under 10 pF at the highest voltages."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Mechanical",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "JEDEC DO-214AA case, plastic moulded over a glass-passivated junction, with built-in strain relief. Terminals are solder plated and solderable to MIL-STD-750 method 2026, and withstand 260 ℃ for 10 s. The moulding compound is rated UL 94V-0; moisture sensitivity is MSL 1 per J-STD-020. Weight 0.10 g. UL file E244458."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Marking",
   "page": 5,
   "text": "The top face carries the Brightking logo, a date code of four characters (YXXX) and the two-letter marking code of its type (KE to QM unidirectional, AE to FM bidirectional). Unidirectional parts add the cathode band; bidirectional parts have none."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Packing",
   "page": 6,
   "text": "Parts ship on 12 mm tape to EIA RS-481: 500 pieces on a 7\" reel or 3000 pieces on a 13\" reel."
  }
 ],
